## Test case docs — required folder structure (no automation)

# Test Case Generation Rules

Always follow this flow when generating functional test cases. Use skill `.cursor/skills/testcase-generation/` for templates, coverage techniques, and TC format.

### When to create the `test/` folder

- **Do not create** `test/` or any `test/[page-name].md` until implementation is complete and you have reviewed:
  - Root `README.md`
  - Relevant `docs/**`
  - The codebase (routes/pages/APIs, `package.json` scripts, env/config)

### Required layout (repo root)

- **Create `test/` at the repository / monorepo root** (sibling to `apps/`, `packages/`, `src/`).
- **Create `test/README.md`** as the index for all test case markdown.
- **Create exactly one markdown file per page/screen/route**:
  - Path: `test/[page-name].md`
  - Filename: kebab-case derived from the **real** page name (route or screen title). Do not invent names.
- **Combine all features on the same page into a single file** (`test/[page-name].md`). Do not split by widget/module when they live on the same page.

Example:

```text
my-project/
├── apps/
├── packages/
└── test/                  ← REQUIRED — markdown functional test cases
    ├── README.md          ← REQUIRED — index
    ├── [page-name].md     ← one file per page/screen/route
    └── ...
```

### Placement rules (must follow)

- **MUST** use folder name `test/` for markdown test case documentation.
- **MUST NOT** put markdown test cases in `docs/`, `plan/`, or inside application folders (e.g. `apps/*`, `src/*`).
- **MUST NOT** use alternative roots like `test-cases/` or a single mega file like `test/all-pages.md`.

### Page-wise scope rules

- **One page → one file**: `test/[page-name].md`
- **Cross-page flows**: only create a separate file when a workflow truly spans pages; reference the relevant page files.
- **API-only scope (no UI page)**: create one file per API resource or endpoint group; name it after that group.


